-- title:
--   Characteristic 2: ord_P(dj)≥ 14 when ord_P(j)=12
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $2$ and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the set of series $\mathrm{qExpand}_K\,d\,(j)$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$, where $j =$ `jqModC K` is $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$ (a unit multiple), i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant; $j$ lies in $F$. Let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ and whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring, with associated normalised order function $\operatorname{ord}_P$ given by minus the logarithm of the height-one-spectrum valuation. Assume $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) = 12$. Then $\operatorname{ord}_P(dj) \ge 14$, where $dj$ is the image of $j$ under the universal derivation $F \to \Omega_{F/K}$ and $\operatorname{ord}_P(\omega)$ denotes the order at $P$ of the coefficient $g$ in a representation $\omega = g\, dt$ with $t$ a uniformiser at $P$ (i.e. $\operatorname{ord}_P(\mathrm{d}j/\mathrm{d}t)$).
--
--   This is the local contribution at a place of the level-$N$ modular function field lying over $j = 0$ with ramification index $12$ — the supersingular point in characteristic $2$ — to the different of the covering $j : X_0(N)_K \to \mathbb{P}^1_K$; classically the exponent equals $14$ there, and only the lower bound is asserted. It feeds the estimate [`ModularCurve.le_six_mul_sum_ordDiff_D_jqModC_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.le_six_mul_sum_ordDiff_D_jqModC_of_lt_five), part of the Riemann–Hurwitz bookkeeping for $X_0(N)$ in characteristic $2$.
